Finding: {"title":"E2E auth bypass ships a hardcoded default secret","severity":"LOW","area":"Authentication / test-bypass hygiene","files":["src/lib/e2e-auth-bypass.ts"],"detail":"getE2eAuthBypassSecret() (line 35-37) falls back to the literal DEFAULT_E2E_AUTH_BYPASS_SECRET ('local-e2e-auth-bypass-secret') when E2E_AUTH_BYPASS_SECRET is unset, and isServerE2eAuthBypassEnabled() only gates on NODE_ENV !== 'production' (not VERCEL_ENV). Next.js production builds (next build && next start, what Vercel runs for every deployed environment including preview/dev/uat aliases) always set NODE_ENV=production, so today this fallback is reachable only under next dev (true local dev), not on any Vercel-hosted environment.","impact":"Currently low risk given Vercel's NODE_ENV=production behavior for all deployed environments, but this is a latent landmine: if the build/start invocation ever changes (custom start script, containerized deploy, non-Vercel host) such that NODE_ENV isn't 'production' while E2E_AUTH_BYPASS=true and E2E_AUTH_BYPASS_SECRET is unset, anyone who knows the checked-in default string can set the hilo-e2e-auth-bypass cookie to that value and mint a super_admin session (getE2eAuthBypassUser defaults to role: 'super_admin' when no user cookie is present).","recommendation":"Require E2E_AUTH_BYPASS_SECRET to be explicitly set (throw/warn loudly if E2E_AUTH_BYPASS=true but the secret env var is absent) rather than silently falling back to a checked-in constant; also gate on VERCEL_ENV !== 'production' / 'preview' as defense-in-depth.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

